WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.948
The cut is ready.

00:00:01.948 --> 00:00:03.895
The script is ready.

00:00:03.895 --> 00:00:06.817
Then the voice service stops responding.

00:00:06.817 --> 00:00:07.790
One producer.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:09.251
Seven waiting jobs.

00:00:09.251 --> 00:00:13.146
And a narration track that will not play.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:17.041
In this demonstration, SideFX's provider-continuity idea becomes visible.

00:00:17.041 --> 00:00:18.989
Keep the creative request.

00:00:18.989 --> 00:00:20.937
Check the permitted alternatives.

00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:22.884
One cannot deliver audio.

00:00:22.884 --> 00:00:24.345
The next can.

00:00:24.345 --> 00:00:28.240
The same script goes to the compatible provider.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.188
Real narration comes back.

00:00:30.188 --> 00:00:33.596
But a response is only the beginning.

00:00:33.596 --> 00:00:35.057
Save the audio.

00:00:35.057 --> 00:00:36.517
Check the artifact.

00:00:36.517 --> 00:00:40.899
Keep the request, provider, and file connected by evidence.

00:00:40.899 --> 00:00:48.203
Now the producer can listen, bring the voice into the cut, and continue the work.

00:00:48.203 --> 00:00:49.663
The provider changed.

00:00:49.663 --> 00:00:51.611
The story stayed hers.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:02.211
Your story is ready to be heard. Every detail has a purpose. Every voice carries the story forward.
